{"event_type":"review","id":"862e38349ea83a49e9a31a3d753021c99e1105f0a76001eb285e7a139320a389","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T06:07:28Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/37461e3f11606d98236b0627b47a0e83c55824cee3c6dc2cdfce29c43500c5bd","sha256":"37461e3f11606d98236b0627b47a0e83c55824cee3c6dc2cdfce29c43500c5bd"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/562f9044fb94f12c203d928ad727e4282e577c41fca11f61bfadd84859980699","sha256":"562f9044fb94f12c203d928ad727e4282e577c41fca11f61bfadd84859980699"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f07fe1945096181abf62a5e070d3b7d47c36f718622864ee1e38eff2c492feb5","sha256":"f07fe1945096181abf62a5e070d3b7d47c36f718622864ee1e38eff2c492feb5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7acb479c63fa29bf0484833493e7da40e337c11904d1b9719746a1ca36173b84","sha256":"7acb479c63fa29bf0484833493e7da40e337c11904d1b9719746a1ca36173b84"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6580d96479a448e5d616ec02693ae7cfbf24218ca023565084730cb420828547","sha256":"6580d96479a448e5d616ec02693ae7cfbf24218ca023565084730cb420828547"}],"attempt_id":"59bd839289450ae83ab4992fbda152cc9b3874e640462d73448382a9e66ac0d5:0:1","base":"69b0de4a1ffdee4c4fee7bd5973cfd401ca04ee7","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"0e71b9891a9d3bf9065f34ea2a7730372b1898cd","body":"**Make publication retry independently of the first service activation.**\n\nIf `state/backfill-rollout.json` is absent when `OnBootSec=1min` fires, `crq-publisher.service` is skipped by `ConditionPathExists`. `OnUnitInactiveSec=1min` is relative to the target service's last deactivation, and a failed condition prevents activation. The timer can therefore stop triggering after boot, so creating the rollout file later waits for a manual start or reboot. ([freedesktop.org](https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/256/systemd.timer.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nUse a path trigger or a periodic calendar trigger that does not depend on the target service's inactive timestamp.","id":"ddad0ba8017a1ccf983d6427a9f12708c6223c95c5527050738bb26c288d2dd3","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/systemd/crq-publisher.timer","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make publication retry independently of the first service activation."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"c601c9a78f07fdb56ee410155120922c5c7ea88f","body":"**Use cgroup cleanup for worker timeouts.**\n\n`crq_slot.py` calls `crq.slot()`, which can launch a detached `_review` child. With `KillMode=process`, a timeout kills only the main service process. The review child can remain active after systemd stops the service.\n\nApply this to both units:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n- KillMode=process\n+ KillMode=control-group\n```\n\n</details>","id":"647906fb788bda17abba9d6cb58e13a025472457774a9f721e1b7cc12f3d40ff","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/systemd/crq-slot.service","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use cgroup cleanup for worker timeouts."}],"head":"530bf49fc63ef852011a3c6c4e24eb659447a0a9","head_tree":"caf2bd1c0f6a76b490442f34307539ee3268e814","input_scope":[{"blob":"3feb985a604753b61d20ff21632acd7b1538f9f3","intervals":[[1,11]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/systemd/crq-publisher.service"},{"blob":"0e71b9891a9d3bf9065f34ea2a7730372b1898cd","intervals":[[1,9]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/systemd/crq-publisher.timer"},{"blob":"c601c9a78f07fdb56ee410155120922c5c7ea88f","intervals":[[1,12]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/systemd/crq-slot.service"},{"blob":"72c5e3e3b981634b30aec766c58b5795f776fe8b","intervals":[[1,12]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/systemd/crq-tick.service"}],"job_id":"59bd839289450ae83ab4992fbda152cc9b3874e640462d73448382a9e